# Repository-root environment: values shared by MORE THAN ONE service.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in this same directory and fill in a real value.
# Both consumers read this one file, so there is nothing to keep in sync:
#   - docker compose reads it automatically (same directory as docker-compose.yml)
#   - backend/src/server.js loads it in addition to backend/.env
#
# Per-service settings (MONGO_URI, JWT_SECRET, PORT, ...) stay in backend/.env.

# Shared HMAC key for the assessment pipeline.
#
# The backend signs a "grant" carrying the client's REAL age, sex and height
# and hands it to the browser; the CV service verifies that signature and takes
# the subject from inside it, so a user cannot edit their age in DevTools to get
# an easier norm band. On the way back the CV service signs the measurements it
# actually produced, and the backend verifies that before storing anything - so
# a score cannot be invented in the browser either.
#
# Both services REFUSE TO START without it: an unsigned result is
# indistinguishable from one a browser made up, so there is no safe default.
#
# Generate a fresh one via terminal (dont reuse the example text, and never commit it):
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#   # or, without openssl:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
#
# Each developer can use their own value. It only has to match between YOUR
# backend and YOUR cv-service - it is not shared across machines.
CV_SIGNING_SECRET=
